<title>GERMANY: German Fin Min says EMU timetable unchanged.</title>
<headline>German Fin Min says EMU timetable unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German Finance Ministry said on Friday Bonn planned no change to the European economic and monetary union timetable with a launch of a single currency in 1999 based on economic data from 1997.</p>
<p>A ministry spokeswoman was reacting to a statement by Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi, who said he thought it was possible Germany would seek a delay.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
